---
import { SITE_TAGLINE, X_URL } from '../consts';
const year = new Date().getFullYear();
---

<footer class="ft">
	<div class="wrap">
		<div class="cols">
			<div>
				<div class="mark">The Tape Says</div>
				<p class="tag">{SITE_TAGLINE}</p>
			</div>
			<div class="links">
				<a href="/research/">Research</a>
				<a href="/data/">Data</a>
				<a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a>
				<a href={X_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">X</a>
			</div>
		</div>
		<p class="disc">
			Everything here is a record of what I measured, not advice. I hold spot positions in the
			assets I write about and say so in the post when I do. Numbers come from public exchange
			and on-chain APIs; the source and the window are named wherever a figure appears, so you
			can pull it yourself and disagree with me on the same data.
		</p>
		<p class="copy">© {year} The Tape Says</p>
	</div>
</footer>

<style>
	.ft {
		margin-top: 88px;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
		padding: 38px 0 50px;
		background: #0a0c0f;
	}
	.cols {
		display: flex;
		justify-content: space-between;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 20px;
		margin-bottom: 26px;
	}
	.mark {
		font-family: var(--font-display), sans-serif;
		font-weight: 700;
		color: #fff;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
	}
	.tag {
		margin: 3px 0 0;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		color: var(--fg-mute);
	}
	.links {
		display: flex;
		gap: 18px;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
	}
	.links a {
		color: var(--fg-dim);
		text-decoration: none;
	}
	.links a:hover {
		color: var(--accent);
	}
	.disc {
		font-size: 0.78rem;
		line-height: 1.7;
		color: var(--fg-mute);
		max-width: 68ch;
		padding-top: 22px;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
	}
	.copy {
		margin: 0;
		font-family: var(--font-mono), monospace;
		font-size: 0.7rem;
		color: #4a5160;
	}
</style>
